      "sourceLink": null,
      "spam": false,
      "statusChangeID": null,
      "value": "2D audio sources should work (we just tested it). You must not add a spatial audio component. You must also not check the box to “Apply 3D Spatialization to AudioSources automatically...” in the build control panel. On your AudioSource, Spatial Blend needs to be on 2D. Finally, the spatialize checkbox should not be checked (this is visible when ANY spatializer plugin is active in the Audio settings). Please let us know if you are running into issues after retrying with the tips above!\n\nAll this said, be aware that 2D audio is often not ideal for VR experiences. It basically puts fixed headphones over your users ears that move with their head and is not a very immersive experience.",
      "viewerReactions": null
    },
